        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Europe weighs Putin’s ceasefire signals and security proposals Europe Issued on: 10/05/2026 - 17:27 Vladimir Putin’s latest comments on potential ceasefire talks are being met with deep scepticism across Europe, with officials questioning both the substance of his proposals and the choice of mediator. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Shirley Sitbon said repeated promises of imminent peace are fuelling doubt, even as discussions continue over Ukraine, NATO expansion and the future of European security architecture. Russia, Ukraine trade blame over ceasefire violations 10/05/2026 Europe Passengers disembark from Hantavirus-hit cruise ship in Canary Islands 10/05/2026 Europe 'Nothing like COVID': Expert urges calm over hantavirus outbreak on cruise ship 10/05/2026 Europe Scottish independence calls grow after Labour losses shake Starmer’s leadership 10/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus poses 'very little risk' to wider public, health expert says 10/05/2026 Europe International evacuation underway as cruise ship passengers return home 10/05/2026 Europe Starmer vows to stay on after local elections deliver losses for Labour 10/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship arrives at Tenerife in Spain's Canary Islands 10/05/2026 Europe Ukrainians mark end of WWII amid fragile ceasefire with Russia 09/05/2026 Europe"
